Substitute $x=1$ and $y=2$ throughout the expression. Keep parentheses around signed inputs:

$$
f(1,2)=\frac{{e}^{2}}{\arcsin\left(1\right)}
$$

Evaluate the inner operations before combining them:

$$
\begin{aligned}
{e}^{2} &=e^{2} \\
\arcsin\left(1\right) &=\frac{\pi}{2} \\
\frac{{e}^{2}}{\arcsin\left(1\right)} &=\frac{2 e^{2}}{\pi}
\end{aligned}
$$

Thus $f(1,2)=\frac{2 e^{2}}{\pi}$.
